# NovaPay Salary Advance — Build Rules

## Context
This is a first-time salary-advance (payday loan) flow for NovaPay, a mobile
wallet in an emerging market scarred by predatory digital lending. Lending is
the highest-trust moment in the app. Every screen must feel honest and humane —
never predatory. Trust beats conversion, always.

## Design system (NovaKit Lite)
- Build ONLY from existing components in `src/novakit` (Button, Card, TextField,
BottomSheet, AppBar, ListRow, AmountText, Toast) and the tokens in
`tailwind.config.js`.
- Do NOT invent colors, spacing, radii, or type scales. 844pxUse the tokens.
- Extend the system only when genuinely needed. When you do, call it out
explicitly in a comment and keep it minimal and consistent with existing tokens.
- Mobile-first. Everything renders in a ~390px frame.

## Product rules (treat as fact)
- Three loan tiers: PKR 5,000 / 10,000 / 15,000. User picks up to their limit.
- Fixed fee = 3% of amount, charged once (NOT monthly interest).
5,000→150, 10,000→300, 15,000→450.
- Single repayment, pulled in full on the user's next payday.
- Total cost of credit AND the repayment date must be clear at the moment of
decision — on the same screen as the Accept button.
- A "haircut" may apply: disbursed amount can be less than requested.
- Decline reasons: credit_score, income_unverified, other.
- Repayment states: on_time, late, default (30+ days).

## Trust rules (the heart of this)
- Show the full, honest total cost before any commitment. No hidden fees, no
fine print, no surprises.
- Never use alarming red, guilt-tripping language, false urgency, countdowns,
or dark patterns that nudge borrowing.
- Decline, over-limit, and late-payment states must be calm, factual, and
respectful — give an honest reason and a clear path forward.
- Prefer restraint: fewer screens, clearer choices. The best error is the one
that never happens.
- Write copy like a decent human talking to a stressed person — plain, warm,
never clinical or threatening.

## Code
- React + Tailwind, built on the existing Vite starter.
- Keep components reusable and tidy. Small, logical commits.
